<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1620corr-lineage> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Fresh narrow lineage: SEN0414 Chapters 16 to 20 corrections"@en ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.3.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1620corr-lineage/1.3.0> ;
    owl:priorVersion <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1620corr-lineage/1.2.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1620corr_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment """1.3.0 (2026-11-26): Objective stage only (one stage per version). Each goal is measured by objectives (26 in all), each metric derived from its goal, each with a counted, derived or judged measurement and a query that reads it, a baseline measured on 2026-11-26 (logs in 08-tooling/lineage13-opening/; the balloon, own-version, spec and page counts from the files named in each query) and a baseline observation. Objectives whose figure is met by absence carry the direction Hold: their figure is read at every observation and can rise. The balloon target is the real count of code slides (117 = 25 + 28 + 27 + 18 + 19); the rdodi objective counts existing files modified or deleted, so new files there are allowed by this objective only where the scope allows them; the allowed folders of the outside-files objective are listed in its query. The objectives are written by the table script 08-tooling/lineage13-opening/objective_make_v1_0_0.py, a lineage's own script, disclosed. Checkpoint dates are forecasts, never deadlines. The goals of 1.2.0 already carry their origin and decider."""@en .

ex:Metric_Obj13_MissionLecture a backlog:Metric ; backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage13 ;
    backlog:metricBaseline "0"^^xsd:integer ; backlog:metricTarget "5"^^xsd:integer ; backlog:metricUnit "chapter" ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 16 to 20 that pass every objective of goals G13_DeckReads, G13_PageRuns and G13_Released, so a lecturer can teach and a student learn from them: 0 -> 5"@en .
ex:CP13_MissionLecture a backlog:ObjectiveCheckpoint ; backlog:checkpointDate "2026-11-28T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ; backlog:expectedValue "5"^^xsd:decimal .
ex:Obj13_MissionLecture a backlog:Objective ;
    rdfs:label "Chapters 16 to 20 that pass every objective of goals G13_DeckReads, G13_PageRuns and G13_Released, so a lecturer can teach and a student learn from them: 0 -> 5"@en ;
    backlog:belongsToLineage ex:Lineage13 ; backlog:objectiveForGoal ex:G13_Mission ; backlog:contributesToGoal ex:G13_Mission ;
    backlog:fillsScope ex:Scope13 ;
    backlog:hasMetric ex:Metric_Obj13_MissionLecture ; backlog:hasSuccessMetric ex:Metric_Obj13_MissionLecture ;
    backlog:hasMeasurementKind backlog:Meas_Derived ; backlog:hasMeasurementQuery "Count of chapters for which the objectives of goals G13_DeckReads, G13_PageRuns and G13_Released are all at target, derived from the observations in the register." ;
    backlog:hasBaselineValue "0"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:hasTargetValue "5"^^xsd:decimal ; backlog:hasTargetDirection backlog:Dir_Increase ;
    backlog:hasCheckpoint ex:CP13_MissionLecture ;
    backlog:hasForecastDate "2026-11-28"^^xsd:date ; backlog:hasForecastRationale "A forecast, not a deadline. backlog_date_plan 1.5.0 could not predict it: this register has no box with effort yet and Lineage12's archive has no pair of consecutive boxes with effort (the tool refused). The date is read from the delivered pace of Lineage12: four chapters from the mission commit (2026-11-26 08:39 Istanbul) to closure the same day, about eight hours; five chapters, two of them needing less work, about eight hours from 2026-11-26 17:00, times the tool's default buffer of 1.5, then the next midnight UTC. To be discussed with the Owner before it is final." ;
    backlog:hasIntentOrigin backlog:IOrigin_SessionDrafted ; backlog:decidedBy backlog:Owner .
